  "question": {
    "text": "Two solid spheres $S_{1}$ and $S_{2}$ of same uniform density fall from rest under gravity in a viscous medium and after some time, reach terminal velocities $v_{1}$ and $v_{2}$ respectively. If ratio of masses $\\frac{m_{1}}{m_{2}}=8$, then $\\frac{v_{1}}{v_{2}}$ will be equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "2",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "4",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{v}=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{r}^{2}}{9 \\mathrm{n}}(\\mathrm{d}-\\rho) \\mathrm{y}$\r\n$\\mathrm{m}=\\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\mathrm{r}^{3} \\cdot \\mathrm{d}$\r\n$\\mathrm{r} \\propto \\mathrm{m}^{1 / 3}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{T}} \\propto \\mathrm{r}^{2} \\propto \\mathrm{m}^{2 / 3}$\r\n$\\therefore \\frac{\\mathrm{v}_{1}}{\\mathrm{v}_{2}}=\\left[\\frac{\\mathrm{m}_{1}}{\\mathrm{~m}_{2}}\\right]^{2 / 3}=(8)^{2 / 3}=4$"
  }
}